[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114641,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cementoblastoma (CB) is a benign odontogenic neoplasm that forms a rounded mass of cementum on the root of a tooth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114642,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9273/0 Cementoblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114643,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.0 &amp; XH4VL1 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of skull or face &amp; Cementoblastoma, benign</p>\r\n<p>2E83.1 &amp; XH4VL1 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of lower jaw &amp; Cementoblastoma, benign</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114644,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> benign cementoblastoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> true cementoma; cementoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114645,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114646,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CB develops on the apical third of a tooth root, most frequently in the posterior mandible, usually on the permanent first molar. Teeth in the mandibular premolar and maxillary molar regions are the second most frequently affected. Involvement of deciduous teeth is rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114647,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CB causes a slow-growing, characteristically painful expansion of the jaw. The associated tooth is vital in about 80% of cases. Root resorption occurs in about two&nbsp;thirds of cases. Cortical bone perforation and tooth displacement are rare {11925541; 28869132}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Radiographically, there is a well-defined, circumscribed, radiopaque or mixed-density mass expanding from the root of the associated tooth. A characteristic radiolucent rim continuous with the periodontal ligament is usually present {11925541}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114648,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CB is a relatively rare tumour, accounting for about 3% of all odontogenic tumours. There is a wide age range, with the highest incidence in the second and third decades of life. There is no sex predilection {11925541; 28869132; 32684315}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114649,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114650,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CB harbours <em>FOS</em> rearrangement and shows FOS overexpression {33653978}, features it has in common with osteoid osteoma and osteoblastoma {31490237}, with which it also shares histological similarity. FOS would be expected to affect the maturation and proliferation of cementoblasts in the same way as it does osteoblasts, but CB appears to have a more indolent growth pattern than osteoblastoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114651,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CB is a calcified mass, usually 20&ndash;30&nbsp;mm in diameter, adherent to and fused with a tooth root.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114652,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CB resembles osteoblastoma histologically. The bulk of the lesion is composed of a mass of dense cellular cementum resembling bone, often with prominent reversal lines, fused with the resorbed surface of the tooth root. At the periphery there are radiating finger-like trabeculae of newly formed matrix, often associated with plump cementoblasts and cementoclasts and vascular immature fibrous tissue.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>This should include cemento-osseous dysplasia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114653,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114654,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114655,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a mass fused to a tooth root; dense mineralization; radiating peripheral matrix; plump cementoblasts; no fibro-osseous component.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114656,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114657,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CB does not usually recur after extraction of the associated tooth and curettage. Recurrence follows incomplete removal or attempted conservation of the tooth {11925541}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:37:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]